;; recordable-coeffect envelope EXACTLY as a runtime dispatch would; the
;; consuming handler reads the framework `:rf.cofx` context key verbatim. This
;; pins that the map form is a first-class step shape and that its `:opts` reach
;; the handler verbatim — the setup step is an ordinary `dispatch-sync`, not an
;; out-of-band channel.
;;
;; The handler reads `[:cofx-key :rf.cofx]` — the framework context key carrying
;; the whole envelope recordable-coeffect map (an UNQUALIFIED keyword, so the
;; corpus's `:cofx-key` auto-wiring does NOT treat it as a declarable supplier;
;; it needs no `reg-cofx`). `ensure-cofx` preserves a caller-supplied
;; `:rf/time-ms` verbatim, so the captured value is the literal the step's
;; `:opts` supplied. A bare-vector seed step precedes it — the two step shapes
;; compose in one config.

